index 39da687..a2d3722 100644
--- a/src/prompts/InvestigatorAgent.md
+++ b/src/prompts/InvestigatorAgent.md
@@ -142,5 +142,26 @@ Because logs are fetched from highly concurrent microservices using a sliding wi
 You MUST verify that any ERROR or failure you attribute to the current packet actually belongs to it. 
 If an ERROR line explicitly mentions a `refId`, `eventId`, or `uid` that does NOT match the Kafka payload you were provided, you MUST completely ignore it. It is noise from a concurrent request.
 
+### KEY FACTS -- END YOUR FINDINGS WITH THIS LIST
+
+The Synthesis Agent writes the casebook from your findings alone: a fact you
+leave out of them never reaches it. End your findings with a section headed
+`KEY FACTS` that lists every packet-specific fact the evidence gives about the
+decision, one fact per line:
+
+- the rule, check or module that rejected the packet, as the logs name it;
+- every identifier the decision involved -- each candidate or matched record,
+  the parent or master record it belongs to, and their EIDs and UIDs --
+  written in full, exactly as logged, never shortened to its first characters;
+- each classification, match result, score, threshold, count and flag recorded
+  for this packet, with its exact value.
+
+After each fact, quote the log line it comes from, or name the tool that
+returned it; quote a line once when it gives several facts. Take these facts
+only from this packet's own lines and tool results, never from a `[context]`
+line or another packet's line. On one last line, `Not in the logs: ...`, name
+the facts the SERVICE CONTEXT asks for that the evidence does not show,
+instead of leaving them out or guessing them.
+
 Determine exactly why the packet failed validation or execution.
 Pass your detailed technical findings and DB rule analysis to the ReviewerAgent.
